    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="0528" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-03T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 3,
                                1920—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>354. With reference to the Legation’s telegram no. 414, dated November 29, you
                    are informed that there appears to be no objection to the Legation’s rendering
                    assistance to Mr. Moss. However, if <pb facs="0529" n="405" xml:id="pg405"/> you
                    judge course doubtful in the premises, you should report by telegraph your
                    reasons and take no action until further instructed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
